# Line endings: LF on every OS for everything the app is built, tested and
# packaged from. A Windows checkout (CI's windows runner included) otherwise
# writes CRLF into the working tree, and a CRLF breaks a shell script outright
# ("/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter" in the .deb/.rpm post-install), the udev
# rule, and any test that reads a file line by line. The repository already
# stores these files as LF; this keeps every checkout that way too.
#
# Scoped to app/ and .github/ on purpose: the reverse-engineering captures
# and legacy files elsewhere are stored as they were recorded.
/app/** text=auto eol=lf
/.github/** text=auto eol=lf

# What a Linux shell or udev reads, wherever it is.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.rules text eol=lf
